and hogs, raw materials and feed ingredients; availability of team members to operate our production facilities; and operating efficiencies of our facilities.","zh":null},{"en":"We operate a fully vertically integrated chicken production process. Our integrated operations consist of breeding stock, contract farmers, feed production, processing, further processing, marketing and transportation of chicken and related specialty products, including animal and pet food ingredients. Through our wholly owned subsidiary, Cobb-Vantress, we are one of the leading poultry breeding stock suppliers in the world. Investments in breeding stock research and development enable us to breed into our flocks the characteristics found to be most desirable.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Walmart Inc. accounted for approximately 19.0% of our fiscal 2026 consolidated sales. Sales to Walmart Inc. were included in all of our segments. Any extended discontinuance of sales to this customer could, if not replaced, have a material impact on our operations. No other single customer or customer group represented more than 10% of fiscal 2026 consolidated sales.","zh":null},{"en":"Our food products compete with those of other food producers and processors and certain prepared food manufacturers. Additionally, our food products compete in markets around the world. We seek to achieve a leading market position for our products through our principal marketing and competitive strategy, which includes:","zh":null}],"competition":[{"en":"Our food products compete with those of other food producers and processors and certain prepared food manufacturers. Additionally, our food products compete in markets around the world. We seek to achieve a leading market position for our products through our principal marketing and competitive strategy, which includes:","zh":null},{"en":"Past efforts indicate customer demand can be increased and sustained through our marketing strategy, strong consumer insights and market analytics and our national distribution systems. The principal competitive elements are advertising, consumer and trade promotions, price, product safety and quality, brand identification, innovation, breadth and depth of product offerings, availability of products, customer service and credit terms.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2026-10-03","items":[{"name":"Beef","val":21662000000,"zh":"Beef"},{"name":"Chicken","val":17564000000,"zh":"Chicken"},{"name":"Prepared Foods","val":10495000000,"zh":"Prepared Foods"},{"name":"Pork","val":6328000000,"zh":"Pork"},{"name":"International","val":2427000000,"zh":"國際"}],"total":56419000000}},"peers":["HRL","CAG","CPB","GIS","ADM"]}}